    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0965" n="871" xml:id="pg871"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    Nos. 985B, and 988, of the 16th and 19th ultimo, respectively, relative to the
                    condition of affairs at Harpoot.</p>
                <p>Your action in the matter of procuring protection of American life and property
                    there is approved. It is trusted that the ordered special protection will prove
                    efficient.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
